    <div class="lp-hero">
      <div><p class="lp-kicker">The CallTeam buying desk</p><h1>How to buy <span>cold calling leads.</span><small>Mobile vs company numbers.</small></h1><p class="lp-intro">Know which number to try first. Work the useful contacts you already have. Buy the contact details you’re missing.</p><div class="lp-actions"><a class="lp-button" href="#call-next">Choose my next number <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="lp-text-link" href="#calling-template">Get the free list template ↗</a></div></div>
      <aside class="lp-brief lb-brief" aria-labelledby="lb-brief-title"><p class="lp-kicker">Our starting rule</p><h2 id="lb-brief-title">Start with the person.<br>Then choose the number.</h2><ol><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Know the buyer?</strong><p>Try a suitable mobile or work direct line.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Still finding the right person?</strong><p>A local company number can help you find them.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Already tried one route?</strong><p>Check the outcome before choosing the next.</p></div></li></ol><a href="#number-types">See the strengths and catches →</a></aside>
    </div>
    <p class="lp-direct-answer"><strong>Which should you call first?</strong> Our starting choice is mobile for a known buyer who works away from a desk, work direct for a known office-based buyer, and the local company number when you need to find who handles the decision. A requested callback or preferred number takes priority.</p>
    <p class="lp-method"><strong>Reviewed {{ guide.reviewed }}.</strong> Practical guidance from CallTeam's list-building, calling and follow-up work. The recommendations are our judgement. Phone-screening details are linked to Apple and Google below. <a href="/case-studies/">See our campaign case studies.</a></p>
  </div></div>
