  <section class="lp-section" id="number-types"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">01 / Make the right first call</p><h2>Mobile, work direct<br>or company number?</h2><p>Each gives you a different route. Choose the one that fits the buyer and the information you have.</p></div>
    <p class="lp-scroll-hint">Swipe the table to compare all three routes.</p>
    <div class="lp-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="lb-number-caption"><table class="lp-table lb-number-table"><caption id="lb-number-caption">Cold calling number types: when to start, strengths and challenges</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Route</th><th scope="col">When we would start here</th><th scope="col">What it helps you do</th><th scope="col">The challenge</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Mobile</th><td>You know the buyer and their work takes them away from a desk.</td><td>Reach the person without starting at the switchboard.</td><td>Unknown-number screening, voicemail, bad timing and data that may no longer belong to the right person.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Work direct</th><td>You know the person and have a credible work line or extension.</td><td>Reach their work phone through a more specific route.</td><td>Old extensions, desk voicemail, hybrid working and transfers that still go nowhere.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Company or branch</th><td>You need to confirm who owns the decision, particularly at a local operating site.</td><td>Find the right role, confirm the location and ask for a transfer.</td><td>Reception, phone menus, shared lines and reaching head office when you need the branch.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <div class="lp-note"><strong>Our take: buy coverage of the right buyers.</strong><p>A mobile label does not fix the wrong company or job title. A company number still has value when it can get you to the person responsible. Keep work direct separate: direct dial does not automatically mean mobile.</p></div>
    <p class="lp-small">Leave a number's type unknown if the source has not established it. Keep the source and check date. A correctly formatted number is not proof that it belongs to the person on your list.</p>
  </div></section>

